#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:206
msgid "Accessing Protected/Private Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:208
msgid ""
"When testing, you can use the following setter and getter methods to "
"access protected and private methods and properties in the classes that "
"you are testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:212
msgid "getPrivateMethodInvoker($instance, $method)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:214
msgid ""
"Enables you to call private methods from outside the class. This returns "
"a function that can be called. The first parameter is an instance of the "
"class to test. The second parameter is the name of the method you want to"
" call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:220
msgid "getPrivateProperty($instance, $property)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:222
msgid ""
"Retrieves the value of a private/protected class property from an "
"instance of a class. The first parameter is an instance of the class to "
"test. The second parameter is the name of the property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:228
msgid "setPrivateProperty($instance, $property, $value)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:230
msgid ""
"Set a protected value within a class instance. The first parameter is an "
"instance of the class to test. The second parameter is the name of the "
"property to set the value of. The third parameter is the value to set it "
"to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:236
msgid "Mocking Services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:238
msgid ""
"You will often find that you need to mock one of the services defined in "
"**app/Config/Services.php** to limit your tests to only the code in "
"question, while simulating various responses from the services. This is "
"especially true when testing controllers and other integration testing. "
"The **Services** class provides the following methods to simplify this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:244
msgid "Services::injectMock()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:246
msgid ""
"This method allows you to define the exact instance that will be returned"
" by the Services class. You can use this to set properties of a service "
"so that it behaves in a certain way, or replace a service with a mocked "
"class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:251
msgid ""
"The first parameter is the service that you are replacing. The name must "
"match the function name in the Services class exactly. The second "
"parameter is the instance to replace it with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:255
msgid "Services::reset()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:257
msgid ""
"Removes all mocked classes from the Services class, bringing it back to "
"its original state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:259
msgid ""
"You can also use the ``$this->resetServices()`` method that "
"``CIUnitTestCase`` provides."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:261
msgid ""
"This method resets the all states of Services, and the "
"``RouteCollection`` will have no routes. If you want to use your routes "
"to be loaded, you need to call the ``loadRoutes()`` method like "
"``Services::routes()->loadRoutes()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:266
msgid "Services::resetSingle(string $name)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:268
msgid "Removes any mock and shared instances for a single service, by its name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:270
msgid ""
"The ``Cache``, ``Email`` and ``Session`` services are mocked by default "
"to prevent intrusive testing behavior. To prevent these from mocking "
"remove their method callback from the class property: ``$setUpMethods = "
"['mockEmail', 'mockSession'];``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:273
msgid "Mocking Factory Instances"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:275
msgid ""
"Similar to Services, you may find yourself needing to supply a pre-"
"configured class instance during testing that will be used with "
"``Factories``. Use the same ``Factories::injectMock()`` and "
"``Factories::reset()`` static methods like **Services**, but they take an"
" additional preceding parameter for the component name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:282
msgid ""
"All component Factories are reset by default between each test. Modify "
"your test case's ``$setUpMethods`` if you need instances to persist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:285
msgid "Testing and Time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:287
msgid ""
"Testing time-dependent code can be challenging. However, when using the "
":doc:`Time <../libraries/time>` class, the current time can be fixed or "
"changed at will during testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:291
msgid "Below is a sample test code that fixes the current time:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:295
msgid ""
"You can fix the current time with the ``Time::setTestNow()`` method. "
"Optionally, you can specify a locale as the second parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/overview.rst:298
msgid ""
"Don't forget to reset the current time after the test with calling it "
"without parameters."
msgstr ""

